<%# Page 2 of the self-report questionnaire — the SPECIFIC questions. Reached
    only by a patient the basic answers on page 1 kept in the running (see
    SelfReportsController#ask_specific?). Nothing answered here can move the
    patient: specific declarations are testimony, and the step they gate reads
    investigator values only. What they buy is a better-prepared first call and
    a place higher in the rep's queue.

    No disclaimer, no exclusions, no extras: all of that was read and answered
    on page 1, and repeating it would only make this page longer. Same rules as
    page 1 otherwise — prompts only, nothing that describes the protocol, no
    verdict per answer. %>
<% content_for :title, t("self_reports.more.title") %>

<div class="container my-5">
  <div class="row">
    <div class="col-lg-7 mx-auto">
      <div class="card health-card shadow-sm">
        <div class="card-header">
          <h1 class="h4 mb-0"><%= t("self_reports.more.title") %></h1>
        </div>
        <div class="card-body">
          <p class="mb-1"><strong><%= @study.display_title %></strong></p>

          <div class="alert alert-info">
            <p class="mb-1"><%= t("self_reports.more.intro") %></p>
            <p class="mb-0 small text-muted"><%= t("self_reports.fill_what_you_can") %></p>
          </div>

          <%= form_with url: study_self_report_more_path(@study), method: :post do %>
            <% @specific_questions.each do |cv| %>
              <%= render "question", cv: cv, current: @declarations_by_variable[cv.id] %>
            <% end %>

            <div class="d-grid mt-3">
              <%= submit_tag t("self_reports.submit"), class: "btn btn-success" %>
            </div>
            <p class="small text-muted text-center mt-2 mb-0"><%= t("self_reports.consent_note") %></p>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
